## Summary

Continue `flex_schema_copy` from fresh `main@75756f3c2966dee1c2fddcd6f8d0d9297f15d550` with the durable owner change-journal foundation.

- add the PostgreSQL `flex_schema_translation_change_journal` with identity sequence, tenant/schema indexes, lifecycle/revision constraints, and root-operation dedupe;
- keep SQLite migration/runtime paths no-op for the journal so lightweight owner tests do not pretend to offer durable ChangeCursor guarantees;
- add one reusable Flex-owned append primitive plus stable deleted-revision helper for subsequent standalone CRUD integration;
- append exact-locale Translation apply changes in the same transaction as the schema/translation mutation, outbox `TranslationTargetChanged` event, and successful idempotency receipt;
- use the durable Translation operation ID as the journal root identity, so retries never create duplicate change evidence;
- suppress journal rows on exact no-op applies because the existing owner `changed` decision remains authoritative.

## Boundary

This PR intentionally journals the already-transactional exact-locale apply path only. A fresh follow-up slice will transactionally retrofit standalone schema create/update/delete onto the same append primitive before ChangeCursor is exposed.

No ChangeCursor/high-water API, host provider registration, registry promotion, tests, Cargo checks, rustfmt, workflows, or CI in this PR.

