Primera parte del hardening de producción: saneamiento del repositorio público y prevención de nuevas exposiciones.

Cambios principales:
- elimina del árbol actual un archivo de credenciales OAuth de Google previamente versionado;
- elimina roles de pago, PDFs desbloqueados, escaneos/contratos y ZIP de respaldo usados durante pruebas;
- amplía `.gitignore` para impedir que estos artefactos vuelvan a versionarse;
- cambia `.env.example` a valores más seguros (`ENABLE_DEV_BOOTSTRAP=false`, secretos vacíos o placeholders explícitos);
- agrega `SECURITY.md` con procedimiento de rotación/purga de historial;
- agrega workflow `security-hygiene` para bloquear secretos/artefactos sensibles en futuros PRs.

Importante: borrar archivos del árbol actual NO elimina el historial. El OAuth client secret expuesto debe considerarse comprometido, rotarse en Google Cloud y luego purgarse del historial con `git filter-repo` o BFG antes de declarar el repositorio completamente saneado.

Este PR no cambia todavía el flujo de autenticación productiva ni MFA; eso se hará en la siguiente subfase después de validar este saneamiento.

Revises and implements R20.3 so Kodepoia remains free to create and free to use.

Zero-cost reference architecture:
- public GitHub repository + standard GitHub-hosted runners;
- two distinct low-authority Ed25519 online keys;
- private seeds stored only as separate GitHub environment secrets `TUF_SNAPSHOT_ED25519_SEED_B64` and `TUF_TIMESTAMP_ED25519_SEED_B64` in `tuf-production-signing`;
- secrets decoded directly in process memory and never committed/uploaded;
- Root/Targets private custody remains fully offline;
- optional KMS/HSM backends remain supported by R20.2 but are never mandatory.

The user completed the local key-generation boundary and returned only the public bundle. Accepted public bundle SHA-256: `4b26dbf702f93e1c2e6f813eae7c22771a06e97fd9d77bd6d57bff1b6c22b1db`.

Integrated public authority:
- Snapshot replacement keyid `fac1c790b4d6dbeb04ca4a803bd80e6fde19127fc7ada34003cef5d6b50506d8`;
- Timestamp replacement keyid `8d81006fd9de63660d74c43b6926ed664b2e9f1bdf81a9556367232533d5a2ad`;
- unsigned Root v2 SHA-256 `7ae909722149fe7f05380f93b7317c99347f8b3c1d102b7b6ddca64bbe1bbe1d`;
- Root v1 and Targets policy remain unchanged;
- Root v2 is intentionally still unsigned and has no production effect.

`docs/roadmap/R20_3_PUBLIC_KEYS.json`, `R20_3_ROOT_V2_UNSIGNED.json`, `R20_3_ROOT_ROTATION_MANIFEST.json` and `R20_3_PUBLIC_PACKAGE_ACCEPTANCE.json` preserve the returned public evidence. Exact-head acceptance independently recalculates keyids, hashes and Root/Targets invariants.

The transition is now explicitly atomic: Root v2 must not be published while Snapshot/Timestamp remain signed by the old Root-v1 online-role keys. Repository tooling therefore performs the remaining manual ceremony as one governed transition: offline Root v2 threshold signing (2-of-3), then Snapshot v4 and Timestamp v4 with the new online keys, preserving the existing bridge expiry `2026-10-08T21:44:18Z`. Only the resulting public `R20_3_FULL_TRANSITION_PUBLIC_PACKAGE.zip` is returned for integration.

A separate `workflow_dispatch` challenge is prepared for `main` after merge. It uses environment `tuf-production-signing`, `contents: read`, no artifact upload and no metadata publication, solely to prove the two GitHub environment secrets match the committed public keyids.

Current manual boundary is blocked until fresh exact-head R20.3/R16.9/R0/Python/UI acceptance passes on the final pre-ceremony head. No private seed, Root key file/path or passphrase is ever requested.

