- canonicalizes undirected edge orientation/order;
- rejects loops, out-of-range endpoints and duplicate edges;
- rejects twist/cardinality mismatches;
- tests exact even/odd twist parity;
- keeps the substrate in the untrusted finite-computation layer; proof status remains exclusively kernel-controlled.

